 deltas, raw user IDs, full future histories, current labels or global sample indexes are supplied to forward.\"], \"task_labels\": [\"is_click\", \"cart\", \"fav\", \"buy\"], \"primary\": \"Validation macro AUC = (is_click AUC + cart AUC + fav AUC + buy AUC)/4. Checkpoint, incumbent, topic gains and final selection all use this rule. Exact ties prefer lower mean Logloss, then fewer parameters, then trial ID. Report every task change; explain trade-offs.\", \"optional\": [\"Literal CONFIG dict for model architecture only; all frozen host parameters are rejected.\", \"Model.training_loss(inputs, probabilities[B,4], train_labels[B,4]) -> finite differentiable scalar; labels supplied only during training. Default is sum of four unweighted BCEs.\"], \"ownership\": \"Edit candidate modules/proposal only. No filesystem/network operations in model source. Imports: torch,numpy,math,typing,copy,functools,collections,itertools,dataclasses,contextlib,unirank,model_zoo. Host owns training, input filtering and scoring.\", \"local_checks\": \"Coding jail has no torch; check syntax/source there. Host trains and scores. Do not install or train inside coding jail.\", \"training\": \"From scratch; same frozen data, seed, epochs, batch, history limit and dense AdamW / embedding Adagrad. Architecture may be rewritten completely. Retain causal controls and account for added parameters/computation.\"}\nCONTEXT KEYS ['history', 'allowed_observation_ids', 'previous_runtime_error', 'trajectory_index', 'incumbent', 'remaining_seconds', 'protocol', 'method', 'budget_scope', 'no_test_feedback', 'knowledge_revision', 'knowledge_review', 'latest_knowledge_usage', 'selection_policy', 'final_assessment_scope']\nallowed_observation_ids [\"baseline-din\", \"g0-r0003-relation_content_counts\", \"g2-r0004-count_shrink\", \"g2-r0006-relation_count\", \"g2-r0006-relation_fixed\", \"g2-r0006-replicas_count\", \"g2-r0006-replicas_fixed\", \"g2-r0007-aligned_early_count\", \"g2-r0007-aligned_early_fixed\",