ntrol exactly reproduced it and is not a new seed. New hypothesis: some long repeated-ad slots overstate independent evidence, and using inverse-concentration diversity d=n\"'^2/sum_a n_a''^2 only as reliability may help preserve useful joint feedback while attenuating concentrated slots. This is a falsifiable proxy explanation; identical IDs do not prove dependent outcomes. At n=8, one repeated ID gives d=1 and alpha=0.2; eight distinct known IDs give d=8 and alpha=2/3. No gain has been measured for this proposal.'\"',nearest_work=[dict(source_ref='trial://g2-r0011-center_count',verification='implementation_checked',difference='Exact starting source SHA25606cd879a5619936c12858a8eac8d8db5937aca08be72c412a2f00adda4bcccba verified in candidate.py; replace only reliability support, retain all learned modules, exposure-weighted moments, user background and raw counts.'),dict(source_ref='g2-r0004-count_shrink',verification='implementation_checked',difference='Read supplied ancestor: inherits count-versus-background shrinkage concept, but applies an identity-concentration support proxy to the centered residual combination rather than introducing new pooling or deleting repeated events.'),dict(source_ref='paper:din',verification='read',difference='Archived primary DIN v4 text lines56-95 and307-336 inspected. Inherit target-local activation and Dice through existing local adaptation; this experiment changes residual historical-feedback reliability, not DIN attention normalization or its mini-batch-aware regularization. No exact DIN reproduction claim.'),dict(source_ref='unirank-code:INFNet',verification='implementation_checked',difference='Pinned forward lines123-170 and benchmark section2.3 inspected: task-mask pooled hubs with layer-wise exchange are an architectural neighbor. No hubs, broadcasts or added task capacity are adopted; proposed intervention operates on an existing fixed-width feedback residual.'),dict(source_ref='unirank-code:EST',verification='implementation_checked',difference='Pinned forward lines119-158 and benchmark section2.3 inspected: sequence/field interaction and pooled prediction are a neighbor, not evidence for diversity shrinkage. No cross-attention stack or feature-specific FFN is adopted. Original INFNet/EST papers are linked but full text unaudited; broad novelty remains unverified.'),dict(source_ref='paper:dmr',verification='read',difference='Only cached author README available; line8 warns its behavior data lack item IDs. This task API supplies previous advertisement IDs, which are used only within visible prefixes. No transfer of missing item inputs or full DMR mechanism/reproduction claim.')],inherited_components=['Unchanged relation-content temporal masks, DIN sums, field embeddings and JointBlock from g0-r0003-relation_content_counts through the incumbent.','Eight disjoint feedback slots, exposure-weighted projected content, four historical task fractions, joint covariance, count channels, user background centering and zero-output-initialized additive residual from g2-r0011-center_count.','Frozen host scratch training, information boundary, selection policy and all existing source receipts.'],proposed_difference='Replace only support in both gate interpolation and covariance coefficient: alpha_s=d_s/(d_s+4) versus n_s/(n_s+4). Here d_s=n_s\"'^2/sum_a n_sa''^2 for known positive nonpadding historical advertisement IDs; each valid unknown/nonpositive/padding ID is a singleton rather than evidence of repeated identity. Empty slot d=0. A sort/run-index/scatter histogram uses O(B*8*L) storage and O(B*L*log L+B*8*L) work, avoiding pairwise LxL identity matrices. Raw n/100, fractions, all exposure-based content denominators and inclusive user background remain unchanged. Both support settings compute the histogram, so same-compute controls share all operations and parameter/RNG order; only the returned support differs. Cross support mode with joint versus factorized moments in four standalone modules. No new learned parameter, external statistic, loss, label, trainable ID lookup or information source. Inverse concentration is a standard statistic used here as a heuristic; no global originality claim.'\"',predictions=['For each occupied slot 1<=d<=n; all unique identified ads or all singleton unknowns give d=n; repeated same known ad gives d=1; empty slots give d=0. Consequently alpha_diversity<=alpha_exposure.','Exposure/joint should reproduce g2-r0011-center_count full validation to runner tolerance with identical initial module state; exposure/factorized should reproduce g2-r0013-inclusive_factorized. Failure is an implementation/calibration concern before scientific interpretation.','Diversity can alter only slots with within-slot known-ad repeats; it must not merge repeats across the eight slots, use current target ID as a history event or react to invalid padding changes.','If the proxy is useful, diversity_joint should exceed exposure_joint and incumbent under equal-weight four-task validation AUC with justified measured cost; report all four AUC/Logloss deltas against DIN, entry, count source and incumbent, even if some tasks regress.','A larger support effect in joint than factorized mode would motivate a paired-seed interaction follow-up, not establish mechanism from this single seed. Any repetition/concentration slices are conditional on an existing authorized host diagnostic interface; do not invent unavailable evaluation outputs.'],falsifiers=['Exposure mode changes initial state, raw counts/fractions, masking or source predictions beyond numerical tolerance; a control mismatch invalidates mechanism inference.','Diversity does not vary from n on actual authorized inputs: the proposed reliability limitation is untested in this data, regardless of synthetic examples.','Diversity_joint fails to beat exposure_joint and incumbent or gains are lost under paired validation repetitions or stronger uniform-shrinkage replacement: utility/identity-specific attribution is unsupported for this implementation.','Any benefit disappears once measured training/inference cost and the smaller count-shrink source are considered: no efficiency claim.','All gains occur in factorized as well as joint mode without a repeated interaction: no evidence that joint coupling is required.','Unknown encoded-ID aliases or a small validation slice explain the apparent improvement; no claim of independent evidence correction is warranted.'],alternative_explanations=confounds+['Extra arithmetic changes wall cost even with equal capacity; comparison to archived controls estimates overhead only when host measurement conditions match.','Diversity may signal a different latent behavior propensity rather than correct reliability. Raw count/fraction inputs already carry some correlated information.','Validation adaptive selection across prior rounds may explain small apparent improvements; deterministic same-seed controls are not uncertainty estimates.'],contrasts=contrasts,cost_plan=dict(estimate_ref='run://r-001 context.remaining_seconds=12342.490186691284 at entry; protocol.estimated_unit_seconds=483.4165504351258, trial_cap_seconds=1208.5413760878146. g2-r0011-center_count measured412.634s; round15 arms400.100-405.271s and about30.4-31.1s validation inference. No local torch/data/training available; do not install. New sort/scatter overhead unmeasured, so allocate600s per full unit (estimate, not a raised cap), 2400s for four arms; all preparation/checks/failures/retries count against the existing43200s hard campaign wall budget.',all_variants_counted=True,attribution_reserve='Reserve1600s for a consequential uniform-stronger-shrinkage replacement and a discriminating duplicate-sensitive follow-up, including diagnostics/failures. The present four-arm factorial is already counted in2400s. Expected parameters remain32,964,809, equal across arms; the smaller source count model has32,288,965 and286.959s measured wall and remains on the quality-cost table.'